To pass audio inputs to vLLM for multimodal inference, you can use the `'audio'` field in the multi-modal dictionary. The input should be a tuple `(array, sampling_rate)`. For example:

```python
inputs = {
    "prompt": prompt_with_audio,
    "multi_modal_data": {
        "audio": (audio_array, sampling_rate)
    }
}
```

This allows vLLM to handle audio inputs as part of the multimodal data.
